<html>
  <head>
    <meta charset='utf-8' />
    <style>
      body { font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto,
      "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif; line-height: 1.6; color: #333; }
      .container { max-width: 600px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; } h1 {
      color: #003087; border-bottom: 3px solid #FFB71B; padding-bottom: 10px; }
      h3 { color: #003087; font-size: 18px; margin-top: 20px; } h4 { color:
      #003087; font-size: 16px; margin-top: 15px; } p { margin: 10px 0; }
      .info-box { background-color: #f0f7ff; border-left: 4px solid #003087;
      padding: 15px; margin: 20px 0; } .warning-box { background-color: #fff9e6;
      border-left: 4px solid #FFB71B; padding: 15px; margin: 20px 0; } ul, ol {
      margin: 0; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 5px; } a { color:
      #003087; text-decoration: underline; } .contact-info p { margin: 0; }
      .footer { margin-top: 30px; padding-top: 20px; border-top: 1px solid #ccc;
      color: #666; font-size: 12px; }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class='container'>
      <h1>We have received your registration details</h1>

      <p>Dear
        {{#if
          mother.firstName
        }}{{mother.firstName}}{{else}}Parent/Guardian{{/if}},</p>

      <div class='info-box'>
        <h3 style='margin-top: 0;'>What we received</h3>
        <p><strong>Date submitted:</strong> {{processedAt}}</p>
        {{#if child.dateOfBirth}}
          <p><strong>Child's date of birth:</strong> {{child.dateOfBirth}}</p>
        {{/if}}
        <p><strong>Certificates requested:</strong> {{numberOfCertificates}}</p>
      </div>

      <div class='warning-box'>
        <h3 style='margin-top: 0;'>What to do next</h3>
        <p>To finish registering the birth, you must go to the Registration
          Department in the district where the child was born to sign the birth
          register.</p>
        <p>The Registrations team will let you know when you can collect the
          child's birth certificate if you have ordered any.</p>
        <p><strong>Find out about:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li><a
              href='https://alpha.gov.bb/register-a-birth#where-to-register'
            >where you need to go to complete the registration</a></li>
          <li><a
              href='https://alpha.gov.bb/register-a-birth#late-registrations'
            >late registration fees</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <section>
        <h3>Who should go to complete the registration</h3>
        <p>If you are:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>married to each other, the father must register and the mother can
            attend</li>
          <li>not married to each other, the mother must register the birth but
            it is not necessary for the father to attend</li>
          <li>not married to each other but the father wants to be named on the
            birth record, both parents must register the birth together</li>
        </ul>
        <p>You do not need to take the baby.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h3>What to bring</h3>
        <p>You need to show:</p>
        <ol>
          <li>Your child's medical book from the hospital or birthing centre
            (sometimes called the green book or immunisation book).</li>
          <li>A valid form of photo identification for each parent who will be
            named on the birth record.</li>
          <li>Your Barbados National ID card, valid passport or other
            government-issued ID if you are a Barbadian citizen. Non-Barbadian
            nationals must show their valid passport.</li>
          <li>Your original marriage certificate if you are married to the
            child's other parent.</li>
        </ol>

        <h4>Parents who are minors</h4>
        <p>If you are a mother or a father and you are under 16 years old, you
          are considered a minor. You must be accompanied by your parent(s) or
          guardian(s).</p>
        <p><strong>If you have a valid passport, you must bring:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>your valid passport</li>
          <li>your original birth certificate</li>
          <li>the child's medical book (green book)</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>If you do not have a valid passport, you must bring:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>your minor's identification card</li>
          <li>your original birth certificate</li>
          <li>the child's medical book (green book)</li>
          <li>an identification letter signed by a Justice of the Peace</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h3>If you need support</h3>
        <p>If you need help registering a birth, for example, you are unable to
          sign the register in person, contact the Registration Department in
          Bridgetown as soon as possible after the child is born.</p>
        <p><strong>Registration Department</strong></p>
        <div class='contact-info'>
          <p>Supreme Court Complex</p>
          <p>Whitepark Road</p>
          <p>St. Michael</p>
          <p>(246) 535-9700</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div class='footer'>
        <p>Government of Barbados - Civil Registration Department<br />
          This is an automated confirmation email. Please do not reply to this
          email.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>